  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Shortwave and backdoor reinforcing cold front\ndropping through ENC tonight with moderate low- mid level \nfrontogenesis. The area of enhanced lift associated with the \nwave and frontal forcing will overlap with an area of moderate \nmoistening and steep lapse rates through late tonight before dry\nair rushes in. While moisture isn't great, the forcing is enough\nto squeeze out some sct rain showers falling through a 6-10k ft\ncloud deck. Very little measurable rain is expected for most \nareas, and with a drying column commencing pre dawn, showers\nwill quickly erode from nw to se and off the coast by daybreak.\n\nBy sunrise Sat, some areas far inland may still see enough \nclearing and decoupling winds to get some frost, though temps\nshould remain safely above freezing limiting impacts. The frost\nadv for the coastal plain counties remains in effect.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A strong surface high will build in over the \nweekend and will be accompanied by a colder than normal airmass.\nThis should support below to well below normal temperatures, \nboth during the day and at night. \n\nThe coldest thicknesses associated with this airmass will \nsettle in late Sat night into Sun morning. With strong high \npressure overhead and good radiational cooling conditions, the \nstage is set for lows in the upper 20s to low 30s for many \ninland areas away from the influence of water. This includes \nareas adjacent to Croatan and Hoffman forest, and the freeze \nwatch that was in effect has been upgraded to a freeze warning \nand expanded to include the interior areas of the Crystal Coast,\nwhich typically outpace even the coolest guidance in these very\ndry airmass regimes. Sun morning may very well end the \nfrost/freeze program for many areas, but for the rest, some \nfrost/freeze potential may continue into early next week as high\npressure continues to support good radiational cooling \nconditions each night in tandem with cont anomalously cold low- \nlevel thicknesses and low TD's in place. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...The aforementioned very dry airmass and low TD's\neach day over the coming week will exacerbate the worsening\ndrought conditions in place across ENC, and fortunately winds\nare not expected to be strong with the high nearby. However,\nfire weather concerns may grow with the curing vegetation\ncombined with low RH values each afternoon.",
